Use "ws client tunnel [command] --help" for more information about a command.
== ws client tunnel conf
Each server with WS_PUBLIC_KEY gets its directory under /etc/ws/tunnel, routes.d and tunnel.conf, written through sudo and readable by all. A daemon whose server has no directory beside values.yml is booted out, its files go, and the daemons left read their files again.

--check fails where a change is due, and changes nothing.

Usage:
